  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (scVI n200, multi-profile, avgpool) achieved 0.650 acc, a large +0.13 jump over the same encoder in single-profile (config_004, 0.520), establishing multi-profile + scVI as the strongest direction. However, we have only tested one aggregation method (avgpool) in the multi-profile setting. Question: config_006 isolates the effect of aggregation (transformer vs avgpool) while holding RNA encoder (scVI n200) and profile setting (multi) constant, giving a clean 1-variable comparison against config_005. Why this is the best next experiment: it directly exploits our strongest evidence to reduce uncertainty about whether a more expressive aggregation mechanism (transformer) can further improve the already-promising multi-profile scVI pipeline. The answer determines whether we should adopt transformer aggregation in all subsequent multimodal experiments, making it a high-leverage decision under a limited budget."
